---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PricePlan from '../components/PricePlan';
import '../styles/public.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pricing" page="pricing"><div class="page-wrap"><header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">PRICING / INDIVIDUAL DEVELOPERS</span><h1>Pay for the routing.<br />Keep your model accounts.</h1><p>One Pro plan. Two ways to pay. Model providers bill you directly for their usage.</p></header><div class="pricing-layout"><PricePlan client:load /><div class="pricing-explainer"><span class="eyebrow">ROOM TO FIND YOUR FLOW</span><h3>Your first route starts the clock.</h3><p>The first 1,000 activated users receive 30 days of Pro. After that, new users receive 14 days. A qualifying activation is your first successfully completed routed model request.</p><h3>No card. No surprise conversion.</h3><p>Try routing before paying. When your free period ends, choose a subscription explicitly to continue. Paid subscriptions renew at the selected interval.</p><h3>Cancel the renewal, keep the time.</h3><p>Cancel monthly or yearly renewal whenever you like. Routing remains available through your paid period. Dashboard and retained history remain accessible afterward.</p><div class="notice"><strong>Launch readiness</strong><p>Checkout is available only after merchant approval and production configuration. Usage allowance and refund terms will be published before accepting payment. No unlimited-routing promise is made.</p></div></div></div><section><span class="eyebrow">THE PRACTICAL DETAILS</span><h2>Good questions.</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Does Pro include model credits?</summary><p>No. Zusal provides routing. You bring your own provider access, and model-provider usage charges remain separate.</p></details><details><summary>What happens if a renewal payment fails?</summary><p>A three-day grace period keeps routing available while you update payment details. If unresolved, routing pauses. Dashboard and retained history remain accessible.</p></details><details><summary>Is the trial the same on monthly and yearly plans?</summary><p>Yes. Your trial eligibility is based on activation, not the billing interval you eventually choose.</p></details><details><summary>What does estimated model cost mean?</summary><p>It is an estimate from available usage metadata and the applicable price data. Actual provider charges may differ. It is not a Zusal invoice or an estimate of savings.</p></details></div></section></div></BaseLayout>
